{title: He Must Increase}
{subtitle: John 3:25–30}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 79}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]A dispute arose between the dis[Dm7]ciples
[Eb]And a Jew about [Bb]cleansing and law [F]
[Bb]They came to John to ask
Who [Dm7]is this one across the Jordan now
[Eb]Bearing witness but now [Bb]baptized [F]
[Eb]Everyone is going to him in[F]stead
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
No one can re[Bb]ceive anything
Unless it has been [Dm7]given from heaven above
I am not the [Eb]Christ I said clearly
But [F]I have been sent ahead of [Bb]him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The one who has the bride is the bride[Dm7]groom
[Eb]The friend stands and listens for his [Bb]voice [F]
[Bb]Rejoicing greatly at the [Dm7]sound
[Eb]This is my joy and it is com[F]plete
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
He must in[Gm]crease
I must de[Eb]crease
He must in[F]crease
I must de[Bb]crease [Dm7][Eb]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]No one can re[Bb]ceive anything
Unless it has been [Dm7]given from heaven above
I am not the [Eb]Christ I said clearly
But [F]I have been sent ahead of [Bb]him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He must in[Gm7]crease
I must de[Eb]crease [F][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
